.TH MOIRA-AGENT-HOOK 1 "August 2026" "moira 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moira\-agent\-hook \- agent activity hook for Claude Code and Hermes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moira\-agent\-hook
.I runtime
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moira\-agent\-hook
is the packaged hook command that Claude Code and Hermes invoke to
record privacy\-minimal agent activity events. The
.I runtime
argument must be
.B claude
or
.BR hermes .
.PP
It reads a bounded JSON payload from standard input (at most 256 KiB;
larger payloads are drained and skipped), extracts only the identity and
model fields, and records the typed activity event into Moira's activity
store.
.SH EVENTS
Claude Code: UserPromptSubmit starts a turn, Stop completes it,
StopFailure fails it and SessionEnd interrupts it. Hermes: pre_llm_call
starts a turn, post_llm_call completes it and on_session_end interrupts
or completes it. Turn events are correlated per prompt through Claude's
prompt_id and Hermes' extra.turn_id.
.SH OUTPUT AND EXIT STATUS
The hook always exits 0 and writes nothing to standard output or
standard error. Any failure (bad JSON, oversized input, store error,
unknown event) is silent, so the agent is never affected.
.SH PRIVACY
Prompts, responses, transcripts, paths, raw payloads, error details,
accounts and secrets are never stored. Only SHA\-256 hashed session and
turn identities, sanitized bounded model labels and UTC timestamps are
persisted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/moira/activity.json
Privacy\-minimal activity store (schema v2; mode 0600, atomic writes
with process\-safe locking; normally
.IR ~/.local/state/moira/activity.json ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moira (1),
.BR moira\-claude\-statusline (1)
